(2) All of the following must apply to the engine family:  
(i) Diesel-cycle engines only;  
(ii) 2004, 2005, and 2006 model years only;  
(iii) Must be an engine family using carry-over certification data from prior to model year 2004 where the NOX plus the HC certification level prior to model year 2004 is below the NOX plus NMHC or NOX plus NMHCE standard set forth in [§86.004-11](https://jjkellercompliancenetwork.com/regsense/details/r40CFR86.004_11). Under this option, the NOX credits generated from this engine family prior to model year 2004 may be used as NOX plus NMHC credits.  
(l) **Additional flexibility for Otto-cycle engines.** If an Otto-cycle engine family meets the conditions of paragraph (l)(1) or (2) of this section, a discount of 1.0 may be used in the trading and banking credits calculation for NOX plus NMHC described in paragraph (c)(1) of this section, as follows:  
(1) The engine family has a FEL of 0.5 g/bhp-hr NOX plus NMHC or lower;  
(2) All of the following conditions are met:  
(i) For first three consecutive model years that the engine family is certified to a NOX plus NMHC standard contained in [§86.005-10](https://jjkellercompliancenetwork.com/regsense/details/r40CFR86.005_10);
(1) Manufacturers of Otto-cycle engines may participate in an NMHC averaging, banking and trading program to show compliance with the standards specified in [§86.008-10](https://jjkellercompliancenetwork.com/regsense/details/r40CFR86.008_10). The generation and use of NMHC credits are subject to the same provisions in paragraphs [§86.004-15 (a)](https://jjkellercompliancenetwork.com/regsense/details/r40CFR86.004_15) through (k) that apply for NOX plus NMHC credits, except as otherwise specified in this section.  
